            <ArticleTitle>[The cause of acute abdominal pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors analyze the structure of acute abdominal pain in the general surgeon &quot;s practice. The article contains the results of an analysis of the frequency of various causes of pain, as well as a description of the most frequent causes of death in acute pancreatitis, cholecystitis, appendicitis, bleeding and perforative ulcer, ileus, strangulated hernia, and acute mesenterial ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
